00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:54,000
Three buddies in Vietnam. Two survived. Only one is really alive.

2
00:13:36,000 --> 00:13:42,000
Jacknife is a drama, war film directed by David Hugh Jones.

3
00:20:24,000 --> 00:20:30,000
A conflict develops between a troubled Vietnam veteran and the sister he lives with when she becomes
involved romantically with the army buddy who reminds him of the tragic battle they both survived.

4
00:27:12,000 --> 00:27:18,000
Joseph 'Jacknife' Megessey, played by Robert De Niro.

5
00:34:00,000 --> 00:34:06,000
Martha Flannigan, played by Kathy Baker.

6
00:40:48,000 --> 00:40:54,000
David 'High School' Flannigan, played by Ed Harris.

7
00:47:36,000 --> 00:47:42,000
Depot Mechanic, played by Ivar Brogger.

8
00:54:24,000 --> 00:54:30,000
Tiny, played by Jordan Lund.

9
01:01:12,000 --> 01:01:18,000
Jake, Veteran Encounter Group Leader, played by Charles S. Dutton.

10
01:08:00,000 --> 01:08:06,000
Jacknife is a 1989 American film directed by David Jones and
starring Robert De Niro, Ed Harris and Kathy Baker.

11
01:14:48,000 --> 01:14:54,000
The film focuses on a complex tension between
people in a close family relationship.

12
01:21:36,000 --> 01:21:42,000
Stephen Metcalfe, on whose play Strange Snow (1982) the
film is based, wrote the screenplay.

13
01:28:24,000 --> 01:28:30,000
Harris was nominated for a Golden Globe Award for his performance.

14
01:35:12,000 --> 01:35:18,000
The tone is emotional.
